.TH EMAIL\-TUI 1 "" "email-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
email\-tui \- full-screen terminal mail reader for email-cli
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B email\-tui
.br
.B email\-tui
.RB { compose | reply | send }
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Interactive reader for the accounts configured with
.BR email\-cli (1).
Started without arguments it opens the account list, then a folder or label
browser, then the message list.
.PP
It requires a terminal. For scripting use
.BR email\-cli (1)
or
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1).
.SH NAVIGATION
Arrow keys or
.BR j / k
move down and up in every list and scroll the reader,
.B Enter
opens,
.BR Backspace ", " Esc " and " q
go back one level,
.B Esc
on the account list (the top level) quits,
.B Ctrl\-C
quits at once from anywhere, and
.B ?
shows the shortcut list of the current view.
.B q
never quits the program and
.B h
is not a help key.  The help overlay and the key handler are made from one
table, so the help lists exactly the keys the view has.
.PP
The browser starts on the
.B Unread
virtual label; the folder list also offers
.BR Flagged ", " Junk ", " Phishing ", " Answered " and " Forwarded .
.B /
starts a content search in the current view.
.SH KEYS
.SS Message list
.TP
.BR j " or " Down ", " k " or " Up
Move the cursor.
.TP
.BR PgDn ", " PgUp ", " Home " or " g ", " End " or " G
Page down, page up, first message, last message.
.TP
.BR Esc ", " q ", " Backspace ", " Left ", " h
Back to the folders or labels; Esc, q, Left and h drop the marks, then the
filter, first.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the message.
.TP
.B /
Filter the list; Tab changes the scope, Esc clears the filter.
.TP
.B Space
Mark the message and step down;
.B x
clears the marks.  The keys that change a message act on the marked
messages, or on the one under the cursor when none is marked.
.TP
.BR c ", " r ", " A ", " F
Compose, reply, reply to all, forward.
.TP
.BR U ", " l
Refresh after a sync, open the rules editor.
.TP
.B *
Star or unstar (toggle the flag), in the list and on the server at once.
.TP
.BR + " and " \-
Mark read and mark unread, at once.
.TP
.B !
Toggle junk, at once.
.TP
.BR d " or " Delete
Delete: move to Trash, or delete for good when the message is in Trash.
Asks first, naming the message by sender and subject; the default answer is
No.
.TP
.B t
Gmail only: pick the labels of the message.
.TP
.B :
Open the action menu: every action that changes state, with its direct key
where it has one.  The menu also holds what has no key: start a background
sync (asks, naming the account and folder), move to a folder or label, toggle
Done (IMAP), and for Gmail archive, restore from Trash, remove the current
label, add or remove a named label.  The menu lists only what applies in the
view: restore in the Trash only, archive in every view but the Archive,
remove the current label in the view of a label only.
.TP
.B ?
Help for the view.
.SS Message reader
.TP
.BR j " or " Down ", " k " or " Up ", " PgDn ", " PgUp ", " Home ", " End
Scroll.
.TP
.BR r ", " F
Reply, forward.
.TP
.B v
Toggle rendered text and raw source.
.TP
.BR / ", " n ", " N
Search the body, next and previous match.
.TP
.B a
Save an attachment.
.TP
.BR * ", " + ", " \- ", " ! ", " d " or " Delete ", " t
As in the list, on the open message.
.TP
.B :
The action menu: toggle Done (IMAP), Gmail archive and remove the current
label, and
.B Save all attachments.
.SS Label browser (Gmail)
.TP
.BR j " or " Down ", " k " or " Up ", " PgDn ", " PgUp ", " Home " or " g ", " End " or " G
Move.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the label.
.TP
.BR Esc ", " q ", " Backspace ", " Left ", " h
Back to the accounts.
.TP
.B /
Search across folders.  The prompt takes text; Tab changes the scope, Enter
searches, Esc cancels and ctrl\-C quits.
.TP
.B :
The action menu: create a label, delete the label under the cursor (only a
label of your own; it asks, naming the label; the default answer is No).
Esc, q and Backspace close the menu and the question.
.TP
.B t
In a Gmail list or the reader: the label picker.  j and k move, Space ticks,
Enter applies, Esc, q and Backspace close it and change nothing, ctrl\-C quits.
.SS Accounts and folders
.TP
.BR j " or " Down ", " k " or " Up ", " PgDn ", " PgUp ", " Home ", " End
Move.
.TP
.B Enter
Open.
.TP
.B Backspace
On the account list (the top level) it does nothing and does not quit; only
.B Esc
quits there.  Everywhere else, outside a text field, it goes back like
.B Esc
and
.BR q ;
in a field it deletes.
.TP
.BR n ", " d ", " i ", " e
Accounts: add, delete (asks), edit IMAP, edit SMTP.
On a Gmail account the
.B :
menu offers "Renew the authorization...": the browser, the address only (for an SSH forward) or a pasted redirect address, as
.B email-cli config reauth
does.
.TP
.BR t ", " c ", " /
Folders: tree or flat view, compose, search.  The search prompt takes text;
Tab changes the scope, Enter searches, Esc cancels and ctrl\-C quits.
.TP
.BR g ", " G
Folders: first row, last row (as Home and End).
.TP
.BR Esc ", " q ", " Backspace ", " Left ", " h
Rules list and rule detail: back (g and G are Home and End in the list);
in the condition editor Esc, Backspace, Left and h cancel the rule and q goes
on to the actions.  ctrl\-C quits at once, also at the questions.
.TP
.BR h " or " Left ", " l " or " Right
Folders, flat view: go up one level (as Esc) and open the row (as Enter).
.TP
.B Esc ", " q ", " Backspace
Folders: up one level in the flat view, otherwise back to the accounts.
.SS Compose and review
.TP
.B Esc
In the compose dialog: asks before it throws away what was typed (the default
answer is No).
.B Ctrl\-C
leaves at once.
.TP
.B :
On the review screen: send the message (asks, naming the recipients; the
default answer is No) or remove an attachment (asks which when there are
several).
.TP
.BR e ", " b ", " a ", " ? ", " q
Review screen (? is the help): edit the headers, edit the body, add an attachment, discard
the draft (asks).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B compose
Open the compose dialog directly.
.TP
.B reply
Reply to a message.
.TP
.B send
Send a message non\-interactively.
.SH FILES
As in
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1),
plus
.I ~/.local/share/email\-cli/ui.ini
which remembers the last account and folder.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR email\-cli (1),
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1),
.BR email\-sync (1)
